## 2. Core Positioning

**One-line pitch:**
> Building small local agent models that run on your own hardware — making frontier agentic capabilities accessible without cloud dependency.

**Expertise pillars:**
1. **Agent post-training** — SFT, RL-adjacent preference optimization, synthetic data generation for tool-calling agents
2. **Benchmark construction** — multi-model consensus, LLM-as-Judge evaluation (EvasionBench, DramaBench)
3. **Open-source shipping** — track record of models and datasets that reach the community (50K+ HF downloads, 400+ GitHub stars)
4. **Agentic systems end-to-end** — from hardware (Unitree Go2 robotics) to social agents (RoboAgent) to CLI tooling (locoremind-social-agent)

**Differentiation from typical ML researchers:**
- Ships working artifacts, not just papers
- Builds at the intersection of local inference + agent behavior
- Research background (ICLR, ICRA) + strong community distribution instinct

